        {
          "id": "7e2c34d418d045babea4c82560238226",
          "index": 18,
          "kind": "task",
          "dueDate": null,
          "startedDate": null,
          "priority": null,
          "title": "variables",
          "task": "here we will setup base system types used for all or most components, as well as some of the data they will use.\r\n\r\nnote, the syntax for a base class is uppercase first letter. \u0027ie Actor\u0022 returns the global type actor, its what you should set your variable as to use a Actor reference. Lowercase is for instance \u0027ie actor\u0022 which returns the actor. for instance.\r\n\r\nActor a = this.actor; would return the actor base of the type.\r\n\r\nif the object has a component that inherits from actor you can get it with this.get_component(type_of(Actor)); which returns the actor (or whatever type you give it). Or\r\nActor a = this.actor;\r\nActor b = a.get_component(type_of(Actor));\r\n\r\nin that case get_component is a function of Actor, which a is an instance of. type_of is a global function which is used to pass a type.\r\n\r\nArrays can take any type even in the same array, and can be accessed via array_name[index] which returns it.",
          "tags": [
            "scripting",
            "cScript",
            "types",
            "data"
          ],
          "files": [],
