        {
          "id": "7ffe86adde734e868accb2ed9e22255b",
          "index": 19,
          "kind": "task",
          "dueDate": null,
          "startedDate": null,
          "priority": null,
          "title": "functions",
          "task": "functions can be created freely with the func keyword a name and any  number of parameters. This then registeres that function for autocomplete, even in other scripts that reference the type the funciton is used in.\r\n\r\nsyntax is\r\nfunc func_name(parameter_type param) : return_type\r\n{\r\n   code;\r\n}\r\n\r\nif no return type is specified you can still return whatever you want it just isnt required.\r\n\r\nfunctions can be abstract and if they are they MUST be overriden in any inherited classes and cannot be called until they are,\r\n\r\noveridden functions are called like this.\r\nthis.base.function_name();\r\n\r\nyou override a function by simply creating one with the same name but without the abstract keyword.",
          "tags": [
            "Scripting"
          ],
          "files": [],
          "requirements": [],
          "flags": {
            "commit": true,
            "build": true,
            "release": false,
            "merge": false
          },
          "isDone": true,
          "isLocked": false,
          "isCollapsed": true,
          "createdAt": "2026-09-10T01:25:37.3311946+00:00",
          "updatedAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"
        },
        {
          "id": "f9f10b41387c43bd8e52cab7a4c997fd",
          "index": 20,
          "kind": "task",
          "dueDate": null,
          "startedDate": null,
          "priority": null,
          "title": "classes",
          "task": "classes are the types that actually get implemented and added to auto complete. classes can inherit from other classes or be inherited from. they can also be set to static (meaning instances CANNOT be made of them, they can be called from anywhere, and the update,start always run even if not instanced on any actors. Also they CANNOT be instanced on an actor and only 1 instance runs ever)\r\n\r\nthey can also be abstract which means they cannot be instanced and MUST be overriden. Each class must have a unique name that doesnt start with a number but does start with an Uppercase letter.",
          "tags": [
            "Scripting"
          ],
          "files": [],
