          "title": "expressions",
          "task": "expressions are ways to compare values, or change them\r\n1 \u002B 2 is an expression that returns 3\r\nx \u002B y returns the sum of 2 variables\r\n1 == 1 returns true\r\n1 != 1 returns false\r\n1 == 2 returns false\r\n\r\n\u0022text\u0022 \u002B \u0022text\u0022 returns \u0027texttext\u0027\r\n\r\nall types (except string and char) should have .str() functions that return it as a string\r\n\r\n\u0022text\u0022 \u002B 1.str() would then return \u0022text1\u0022",
